  "Openers" -> {
   "PrimaryExamplesSection" -> Open, "ExampleSection" -> {"0" -> Open}}, 
  "NewStyles" -> True, "CitationPopupData" -> {$Failed, ""}, "ShowCitation" -> 
  False, "RootCaptions" -> "", "HeaderCoreAreaLink" -> {}, 
  "Metadata" -> {
   "built" -> "{2026, 9, 7, 23, 6, 42.423043}", 
    "history" -> {"2.0.0", "", "", ""}, "context" -> "MagneticTB`", 
    "keywords" -> {
     "high-symmetry antiferromagnet", "type-IV magnetic space group", 
      "spin-space group", "spin-orbit coupling", "continuous symmetry", 
      "C infinity", "initfromrep"}, "specialkeywords" -> {}, 
    "tutorialcollectionlinks" -> {}, "index" -> True, "label" -> 
    "Magnetic T B Tech Note", "language" -> "en", "paclet" -> "MagneticTB", 
    "status" -> "None", "summary" -> 
    "Consider the tetragonal antiferromagnet with magnetic space group \
124.360, P_c4/mcc. Its 32 operations generate two sites, at z=0 and z=1/2, \
with opposite moments. We compare the Hamiltonians and bands with and without \
spin-orbit coupling (SOC). Keep all px, py, and pz spin states so that onsite \
SOC can mix the different orbitals and spins. With SOC, spin rotates together \
with the spatial operation. Pass the complete magnetic space group to init, \
then calculate the onsite term and the nearest-neighbor hopping between the \
two layers: The two layers have opposite moments. The 6 by 6 matrix below is \
the onsite block of the z=0 layer, with rows and columns ordered as \
{pxup,pxdn,pyup,pydn,pzup,pzdn}:", "synonyms" -> {}, "tabletags" -> {}, 
    "title" -> 
    "High-symmetry tetragonal antiferromagnet: spin symmetry and SOC", 
